Package: fabos-voice
Version: @DISTRO_VERSION@-@PKG_REVISION@
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Maintainer: @VENDOR_NAME@ <support@patienceai.in>
Homepage: https://fabos.patienceai.in
Depends: python3, python3-numpy, pipewire-bin | pulseaudio-utils, pocketsphinx, pocketsphinx-en-us, whisper.cpp, espeak-ng, libnotify-bin
Recommends: fabos-agent, sox
Description: @DISTRO_NAME@ voice — "Hey Fab" wake word, speech-to-text, spoken narration
 Talk to @DISTRO_NAME@. An always-on, fully offline wake-word listener
 (pocketsphinx keyphrase spotting) waits for "Hey Fab"; what you say next is
 transcribed offline with whisper.cpp (tiny.en model shipped in
 /usr/share/fabos/voice) or, when you configured a cloud provider and allow
 it, through the agent's speech endpoint. The request goes to the
 @DISTRO_NAME@ agent and the daemon narrates every step, asks for approvals
 by voice and speaks the reply. Ships the fabos-voice CLI (listen-once, say,
 status, wake on|off) used by every @DISTRO_NAME@ UI, and the per-user
 fabos-voiced service. Offline text-to-speech is espeak-ng; the human-like
 Indian-English voice needs a cloud speech provider key, set in Fab AI Controls.
